  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'A light is an input to the shader of every surface it reaches. A Directional light uses only its direction. A Point light uses a position and a Range. A Spot light uses a position, a direction and a cone (Inner / Outer Spot Angle). Here each light reaches only its own arch.


    <b>Predict:</b> You move the Directional light 1 km away, and then rotate it. What changes on its arch each time?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Move, then rotate the Directional light.

    2. Do the same with the Point light and the Spot light.

    3. Note which change matters for each type.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Light-Values (the light sources to look up)</color></size>'
